{"url": "https://junioracademics.unibe.ch/doctorate/pursuing_a_doctorate_at_the_university_of_bern/index_eng.html", "final_url": "https://junioracademics.unibe.ch/doctorate/pursuing_a_doctorate_at_the_university_of_bern/index_eng.html", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-26", "text": "Doctoral Subjects | University of Bern\nHomepage\nMenu\nInhalt\nKontakt\nSuche\nSprachwahl\nWichtige Seiten\nPortal for Junior Academics\nMenu \u00f6ffnen\nMenu schliessen\nPortal for Junior Academics\nDoctorate\nHomepage\nDoctorate\nPursuing a Doctorate at the University of Bern\nShould I Pursue a Doctorate?\nFirst Steps towards a Doctorate\nGoals of a Doctorate\nDoctoral Agreement\nDoctoral Studies\nJoint Doctorate Programs (Cotutelle de th\u00e8se)\nSupervision\nAfter the Doctorate\nFunding\nSkills\nAdvice\nAbout Us\nPortal\nUniBE\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nPursuing a Doctorate at the University of Bern\n\u00a9 University of Bern\nAre you interested in conducting independent research and want to start a doctorate at the University of Bern?\nThe University of Bern is one of Switzerland\u2019s leading universities and is renowned for its excellent achievements in teaching and research. Its eight faculties and various strategic centers offer a wide curriculum. Doctoral candidates at the University of Bern benefit from superb research conditions and an excellent infrastructure. The university has a strong international orientation and attracts researchers from all over the world, offering abundant opportunities for scientific knowledge-sharing and networking, particularly for young researchers.\nSupervision\nSupervision\nDoctoral candidates at the University of Bern are supervised by highly qualified researchers. Application of the dual control principle means that every doctoral candidate will have (at least) two supervisors. Furthermore, the University of Bern has various funding schemes and research-integrated study courses on offer that provide targeted support to doctoral candidates.\nDual Supervision\nCity of Bern\nCity of Bern\nThe University of Bern is closely connected to the Swiss federal capital Bern. The location boasts not only a wide range of educational, cultural and sporting activities, but also a high standard of living and high environmental quality.\nThis is Bern\nDoctoral subjects\nHere you will find a list of all doctoral subjects available at the University of Bern, from A to Z.\nAn A-Z of doctoral subjects\nAn A-Z of doctoral subjects\nArchaeology\nBusiness Administration\nCellular and Biomedical Sciences (med./nat./vet.)\nChemistry and Molecular Sciences\nClimate Sciences\nCognition, Learning and Memory\nGerman Language and Literature\nDigital Humanities\nEcology and Evolution\nEconomic Globalisation and Integration\nEnglish Language and Literature\nEarth Sciences\nEducation\nFrench Language and Literature\nGender Studies\nGeography\nGeography and Sustainable Development\nHistory\nGlobal Studies\nHealth Sciences (hum./med./vet.)\nHuman Medicine\nComputer Sciences\nInterdisciplinary Cultural Studies ICS\nIslamic Studies and Oriental Literature\nItalian Language and Literature\nJewish Studies\nCommunication and Media Studies\nArt History\nLanguage and Society\nLinguistics\nMathematics\nMolecular Life Sciences\nMusicology\nPhilosophy\nPhysics/Astronomy\nPolitical Science\nPrecision Engineering\nPsychology\nPublic Administration\nLaw\nReligious Studies (theol.)\nSlavic Languages and Literatures\nSocial Anthropology\nSociology\nSpanish Language and Literature\nSport Science\nStatistics\nCriminal Justice\nTheatre and Dance Studies\nOld Catholic Theology\nProtestant Theology\nAdministrative Science\nCentral Asian Studies\nClassical Philology (special qualification in Greek or Latin)\nCommunication and Media Studies\nDental Medicine\nEconomics\nDental Medicine\nEastern European Studies\nScience of Religion (human.)\nVeterinary Medicine\nFind out more\nDoctorate at the Faculties of the University of Bern\nFaculty of 